{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487709-new-drowned-legacy-in-hunter-5","id":1487709,"title":"New Drowned Legacy in Hunter 5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-24T02:53:49-07:00","id":1487709,"title":"New Drowned Legacy in Hunter 5?","content":"So, the new Hunter the Reckoning corebook has three really interesting Vampire antagonists, two based in Mexico, one of which is the sort of monstrosity Tzimisce would leave behind them, and one, a conspiracy of flesh-and-spirit eating people, based in the Philippines. <br /> <br /> The second Mexican antagonist is a wily, charismatic crime lord and human trafficker called Efraim. <br /> <br /> Based in Tlaxcala, he provides blood and goods to local vampires (probably, he is a part of the Circulatory System) and maintains a powerbase in the drug cartels. <br /> <br /> He once worked for the Blood Cults (the Sabbat?), but he now works for the invading &quot;Establishment&quot; (clearly the Camarilla). <br /> <br /> His true aim, however, is to take down the local vampiric hierarchy and resurrect his old bloodline, the &quot;Luminous Ones&quot; (Tlahuelpuchi). <br /> <br /> He shows some unusual powers, such as Fire Resistance (fire dealing only superficial damage), vomiting a cloud of blood and fire, and turning into a pillar of fire that deals two levels of Aggravated Damage per turn. He can also shapeshift in a coyote. <br /> <br /> So, it seems reasonable to say that we are seeing a new Drowned Legacy here (for those unfamiliar with the concept, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Drowned_Legacy\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Drowned_Legacy</a> ). <br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see if these new Bloodlines will be given a more fleshed out form: OPP and Martin Ericsson were keen to use them, and they popped out in V5 Core, Chicago by Night 5, and Cults of the Blood Gods. <br /> <br /> However, I haven't seen them mentioned so far in products of the &quot;Achilli run&quot; of V5. Hope we will see more about them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 07-24-2022, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T03:38:54-07:00","id":1487713,"title":"","content":"Any idea who wrote Ephraim? He's kinda every borderwall proponents prejudices regarding those south of the US-Mexican border given vampiric form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","user":"BadFurryFanFic","date":". 07-24-2022, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T03:43:10-07:00","id":1487714,"title":"","content":"The author is Mario Orteg\u00f2n, Mexican: he was credited by Justin on Twitter some weeks ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T03:51:39-07:00","id":1487717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487709-new-drowned-legacy-in-hunter-5?p=1487714#post1487714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The author is Mario Orteg\u00f2n, Mexican: he was credited by Justin on Twitter some weeks ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok. Bold choice I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T05:13:11-07:00","id":1487722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487709-new-drowned-legacy-in-hunter-5#post1487709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He shows some unusual powers, such as Fire Resistance (fire dealing only superficial damage), vomiting a cloud of blood and fire, and turning into a pillar of fire that deals two levels of Aggravated Damage per turn. He can also shapeshift in a coyote.<br /> <br /> So, it seems reasonable to say that we are seeing a new Drowned Legacy here (for those unfamiliar with the concept, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Drowned_Legacy\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Drowned_Legacy</a> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>What crosses my mind is that to develop such powers through a Blood Magic (Lure of Flames) + Protean combination shouldn't be hard, on the contrary kind of simple even.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, in my own games the Harbingers of Skulls are themselves a (mostly mesoamerican) Drowned Legacy with some fun tricks hidden in their sleeves and a dubious, elusive connection to either Baali, Cappadocians, Nosferatu or even all of the three.<br /> <br /> (And a liking for the use of <a href=\"https://www.redbubble.com/i/poster/Oingo-Boingo-design-by-votsis/63424057.LVTDI\" target=\"_blank\">iconography</a> from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yhN8SdulOFc&amp;list=RDEMfnovtiltqd_RSY_DPyIgoA&amp;index=2\" target=\"_blank\">Oingo Boingo</a> as a cypher/callsign of sorts in dealing with their many ignorant rivals/marks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-24-2022, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T07:00:15-07:00","id":1487728,"title":"","content":"&quot;Luminous Ones&quot; could refer to the Serpents of the Light. They would have Protean and their own forms of blood magic.<br /> <br /> They could certainly be a Drowned Legacy, too, however. I always liked the vague hints that the Samedi might be a Drowned Legacy, too. There's lots of room for them to be something weird and new, but they could also be things we've already seen and not properly understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}